      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Important Sessions of the Indian National Congress"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indian National Congress (INC) was established in December 1885 at Bombay, with W.C. Bonnerjee serving as its first President.",
        "Lord William Bentinck was appointed as the first Governor-General of India under the Charter Act of 1833.",
        "The Government of India Act 1858 replaced the title of Governor-General with Viceroy, making Lord Canning the first Viceroy of India.",
        "The historic 1929 Lahore Session passed the resolution for Purna Swaraj (Complete Independence) under Jawaharlal Nehru's presidency.",
        "The National Anthem 'Jana Gana Mana' was sung for the first time at the 1911 Calcutta Session of the INC."
      ],
      "id": "ifc9bfr"
    },
