    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "First Female INC President: Annie Besant (1917, Calcutta); First Indian Female President: Sarojini Naidu (1925, Kanpur).",
        "Lord Ripon introduced Local Self-Government in 1882 and repealed the controversial Vernacular Press Act.",
        "Lord Dalhousie introduced the Doctrine of Lapse, inaugurated the first passenger railway line (1853), and started the electric telegraph in India.",
        "Badruddin Tyabji presided over the 1887 Madras Session as the first Muslim President of the INC."
      ],
